    """Check the (LB) 4-point property in O(n^2) bit operations.

    For all positions a < b < c with ac in E and ab not in E,
    there exists d < a with db in E and dc not in E.

    For a fixed a, sweep b from a+1 to n-1 while maintaining
      D_a(b) = { d < a : b in N(d) }
      U_a(b) = union of N(d) over d in D_a(b)
    incrementally (one OR per new witness).  Then:
      - if D_a(b) is empty: any c > b with c in N(a) violates;
      - otherwise: any c > b with c in N(a) \\ U_a(b) violates.
    """
    for a in range(n):
        va = order[a]
        Na = masks[va]
        union = 0
        empty = True
        for b in range(a + 1, n):
            vb = order[b]
            if Na >> vb & 1:
                continue  # ab in E: nothing to check
            # ab not in E: check the 4-point property
